  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1100 AM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nLarge scale ridging and high pressure will largely remain in \nplace through the day Wednesday. However, by Wednesday night the\nquiet dry pattern appears to get broken up a bit as the ridge \nmoves out to the east allowing a few shortwaves to swing through\nwith the first being Wednesday night. Moisture may end up being\na concern with this system but this will bring at least light \nprecip chances back to the area. Some brief and weak ridging \nreturns as we head into next weekend with the next \nshortwave/trough swinging through Saturday into Sunday. \n\nThis will be a stronger system based on current forecast with \nthe potential for a closed low situation depending on the \ndevelopment. However, this looks to be a stronger system with \nwarm temperatures with the southerly winds ahead of the front \nand colder temperatures behind the front. In addition, expect \nthis to hold a fairly strong chance for precip and even a chance\nfor storms. If we can get enough instability and the timing is \nright I would not rule out strong to severe storms given the \nlikelihood for a very high shear environment. Beyond next \nweekend things really diverge in models as one might expect \ngiven how far out that is but also because of the uncertainty of\nhow the upper low will play out. Otherwise models remain fairly\nsimilar into next weekend.\n\nKuroski",
